export anchor TeaHouseStyle:
    number: 171
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Tea house
    idea: The dashboard is laid out like a quiet tea room, where panels are tatami mats edged in dark cloth, a wooden beam carries the header, a bamboo pole divides the room and progress grows as bamboo segments in tea green and wood.
    base: light
    palette:
        shoji: #f6f2e4, the page under a 160 by 96px lattice
        lattice: #ddd1b3, lattice lines, never text
        tatami: #e9e2c3, mat panels with a fine woven texture
        straw: #d9cf9f, rules inside mats
        heriCloth: #3e4a26, the dark mat edges
        wood: #6e4a2c, the header beam and the plaque frame
        lightWood: #b08a5e, hairlines and unfilled bamboo segments
        ink: #2a2418, text
        softInk: #5a4a33, meta and dates
        teaGreen: #3f5a1f, headings, the primary button and On track
        youngBamboo: #a3b56f, last-week stalks
        bamboo: #4d6a28, this-week stalks and filled segments
        roasted: #8a4a12, At risk
        persimmon: #9b2c1e, Behind and overdue
        focus: #2f5bb0, the focus outline
    type:
        Text uses Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu Mincho, Noto Serif CJK JP, Iowan
        Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Georgia. Labels and controls use
        Hiragino Sans, Yu Gothic, Noto Sans CJK JP, system-ui. Total
        figures are 52px regular mincho, the greeting 34px at 500 tracked
        0.04em, project names 19px, body 16px at 1.7, and headings 13px
        gothic semibold tracked 0.3em with a trailing wood hairline.
    layout:
        A dark wood beam header holds the widely tracked brand, a paper
        search field, a paper New project button, an outlined bell and the
        user name. A pale sliding-door strip below is the nav, each item
        framed by lattice lines, Home on tatami with a dark cloth underline.
        The room is three columns, a wide stack, a vertical bamboo pole
        with dark nodes, and a narrow stack. The wide stack has the
        greeting mat with the date and a wood-framed overdue plaque, four
        square half mats for the totals with cloth on the left and right,
        and the projects mat listing each project with name and meta, a
        row of ten bamboo segments filled to the percent, the percent with
        tasks done and the status. The narrow stack has vertical mats for
        the chart and the recent activity. The chart draws each day as a
        rounded bamboo stalk with dark nodes every three tasks, young green
        last week and deep green this week. Below 960px the pole turns
        horizontal and everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit with generous steps of 24 and 40px. Mats have 24 to 28px padding.
    density: Sparse and quiet, with even rhythm and plenty of empty mat.
    corners: Square mats and 2px controls. Only bamboo is rounded.
    borders: 8px heri cloth on the two long sides of each mat, 1px straw rules inside, a 4px dark beam edge.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from the woven straw texture and the bamboo gradient.
    icons:
        Simple natural shapes beside words. A leaf for On track, an
        outlined triangle for At risk, a solid square for Behind and a
        clock ring for Overdue. Line icons for search and the bell.
    focus: A 2px focus blue outline offset 4px, white on the wood beam.
    tone: Calm and brief, such as This week, Fourteen days and Recent.
